		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4688&amp;p=35019#p35019"><![CDATA[
Hello, this is not connected to ras directly, but i believe to slot hold time. I have seen few reports of advanced users on this forum with same problem. You must be monitoring multi site frequency or capacity plus two site or something in this style - which constantly changes slots, even between two modulations. Ras is often persistand on those type of systems. It happens qso is missed sometimes. This happens in scan mode or without. <br><br>I have already asked developers, if there is possibility to make an option ts filter time to 1 second, like it was on older firmwares and i dont know the reason they have changed to to 2sec max, but itn this case its causing troubles.<br><br>I have two baofeng 1801, one with older fw - works perfectly, newer ones with filter time 2 sec misses qsos sometimes.<br><br><strong class="text-strong">This is not only connected to non ham</strong>, the same is if you monitor duplex hotspots and want to monitor both slots fast. If you monitor both slots and some modulation stops on slot 1 for example (on second slot also some qso) it takes two seconds to start monitoring both slots and "open" slot 2 modulation. For those, who want to jump.constantly from one to another ts is this setting not convinient at all.<br><br>Please if you change option ts filter time to 1 sec or 0.5sec minimum, to test at least if this is the reason. I think that also effect scan speed, as older fw scans faster but very rarely misses qso, newer ones have much more problems. <br><br>I think this is a point that can be improved, as it worked better in the past.<br><br>I hope you understand my point. <br><br>73<br>S58sms<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2305">S58SMS</a> — Mon Jan 06, 2025 7:50 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
